  "title": "# Build: apps-control-surface (Current profile) - finish molly-console-commands s6-s7, NEXT in queu…",
  "asked": "# Build: apps-control-surface (Current profile) - finish molly-console-commands s6-s7, NEXT in queue ## What Brett said (voice, Nov 3-4 2026) Nov 3 (addendum to molly-console-commands): \"Put EVERY app on the API, MCP and CLI\" - Molly, axHub web, AmberX, and every future app via the framework template; plus an apps_list read. Never built (#288 report: 'Not done yet: s6-s7'). Nov 4: Amber couldn't open AmberX's notes/to-dos for him because the console has no AmberX screen and AmberX has no control surface. \"All right, move that to next in queue.\" Book to a free named agent (Ping Paulie, else Polo). Register id `apps-control-surface` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. **Fable** for the shared contract (s1), Opus for the rest (standing order, no approval). ## Do - s1 (Fable) Generalise the console's control surface (console_open/show/action/dialog/settings, control_list of screens/dialogs/settings/actions/nav/clients) into a framework contract every app implements (same messages Molly already relays from #288). `apps_list` read: every app, its clients online, its screens. - s2 **AmberX** (web + Android shell): screens (Notes, To-dos, Lists, Inbox, Voice, Settings...) openable via MCP/API/CLI (`app_show {app:'amberx', target}`), plus its existing items tools. So Amber can 'open your to-dos' on his phone. Uses console-wake/AmberX open_url when the app isn't in front. - s3 **Molly** (switch frames, layouts, dock panes, banners, what's on screen), **axHub web** (approvals, passes, services), **Expenses**, **Gizmo** - same surface. Framework app template + `axf init` get it automatically. - s4 Voice commands per the new-app rule (forFramework apps). Follow Amber's console_show accepts `app:` so mentions open in the right app. - Tests, PRs merge when CI green, redeploy the apps. Never leave tsc/vite/playwright running. Report `_claude/builds/reports/apps-control-surface.md`. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
